# Server (Hono + Bun)

The API is a Hono app on Bun. `createApp(opts?: { runner?: PipelineRunner; ai?: OpenRouterClient })` in `src/server/app.ts` is the factory — tests call it with `app.request()`. Inject a recording `runner` in tests; omit it to use `noopRunner`. Inject a stub `ai` for routes that call a model inline (`POST /api/documents/:id/draft-type`); omit it and those routes reject with "No AI client was provided to createApp" rather than reaching OpenRouter. Do not add Express or Fastify.

## Routes

- One module per resource under `src/server/routes/`. Register with `app.route("/api/...", routes)`.
- Register static path segments before parameterized ones (`GET /unread-count` before `POST /:id/read`) so the static name is not captured as an id.
- Parse JSON with Zod `safeParse`. Invalid body → `400` + `{ error: zodIssueSummary(...) }` from `src/shared/zod-issue-summary.ts`. Do not return a flat `"Invalid request body"`. Do not hand a raw body to Mongo.
- `GET /api/search?q=` (`src/server/routes/search.ts`) serves the command palette: the query is regex-escaped before matching (untrusted input must only literal-match), joined lookups batch with `$in`, and results cap at 8 per group.
- Map driver docs through the shared schema before `c.json`.
- Response and list-row shapes live in `src/shared/schemas/api.ts` (`documentListResponseSchema`, `engagementListResponseSchema`, `engagementDetailSchema`, `metricsSchema`, `portalStateSchema`) and `src/shared/schemas/inbox.ts` (`inboxThreadsResponseSchema`, `inboxMessageResponseSchema`) and are parsed on the way out. Conversation messages write only through `src/server/db/messages.ts` (`insertMessage` / `listMessages` / `markMessagesRead`) — no route inserts into the messages collection directly. The client parses the same schemas, so a row gains a field in exactly one place. Do not declare a row shape inside a route module.
- `app.notFound` stays JSON `404`. Do not leak stack traces to clients; log the cause server-side.
- A route that calls a model or reads a stored file inline returns the real underlying message (`502` for an upstream failure), never a generic "something went wrong". Log it too.

## Config

`src/server/config.ts` is the only module that reads `process.env`. Feature code imports `config`. New env vars: add to `config`, `.env.example`, and `keeping-docs-fresh` in the same change. OpenRouter key and model live there (`OPENROUTER_API_KEY`, `OPENROUTER_MODEL`).

## Pipeline

`createRunner({ ai })` fires `runPipeline` in the background. Stages are quality → classify → extract (`src/server/pipeline/stages.ts`). Unclassified documents can `POST /api/documents/:id/draft-type` for a non-persisted schema proposal. A reviewer overrides a mis-classification with `POST /api/documents/:id/reclassify` (`needs-review` / `unclassified` only): the route flips the document to `extracting` and `runner.startReclassify` fires `reclassifyDocument` — an extract-only continuation (classification written as the human's decision, confidence 1; classify never re-runs) that relinks the checklist item and shares the pipeline's failure lane. Production `src/server/index.ts` wires the real OpenRouter client; tests inject a stub `ai` / recording `runner`.

## Export

`src/server/export/engine-map.ts` owns the tax-engine contract: `ENGINE_LINE_MAP` (filing type → engine lines), `mapExportLines(filingType, trustedDocuments)` (the one mapping, honoring `editedValue ?? value`), and `exportPayloadJson`. Every producer — the route builder and the demo seed — goes through those; a second copy of the mapping is how a demo book starts showing figures the live path would not produce.

A **draft** export is a derived view of the currently trusted documents, not history: `GET /api/engagements/:id/export` remaps it on read (`getCurrentExportForEngagement`), so a document trusted after the draft was built reaches its line without the reviewer hunting for a rebuild control. The rebuild persists because `POST /api/exports/:id/confirm` sends the stored record — the reviewer must send exactly what they saw. A **sent** export is immutable and is returned verbatim. Unmapped lines stay `null` and the screen says how many; a `0` in an engine line nobody grounded would be an invention.

## Scripts

`scripts/seed.ts` seeds or `--reset`s the demo book. `scripts/generate-demo-docs.ts` regenerates `demo-docs/`. `scripts/smoke-llm.ts` (`bun run smoke`) boots the real app + OpenRouter client and is **not** in the bun test gate.

## Anti-patterns

Reading `process.env` in a route. A second HTTP framework. Side-effecting DB connects at import time in a way tests cannot isolate. Swallowing driver errors into a generic 200.
